do you have big goals that you want to  accomplish this year i recently made a  video on how to make 2022 your best year  but in this video i wanted to dive  deeper than that and actually talk about  the specifics of how you go about  carrying out those goals because we can  sit down and plan out our goals and  write down lists all we want to but when  it comes to actually carrying those  things out and putting them into  practice that's when the going gets  tough so in this video i want to share  with you five lessons that i have  learned through building our own home  and hopefully those lessons can be  helpful to you so you can achieve your  goals in 2022. lesson number one to eat  an elephant you have to take it one bite  at a time we built our home as our own  general contractors with no prior  building experience and we did have some  help for major things like foundation  for example but we did a great majority  of the work ourselves and this quickly  began to feel draining a daunting task  not only physically but also emotionally  and these were the words of my mentor  when i broke down because i felt like  there was no end in sight  she said to eat an elephant you have to  take it one bite at a time sure these  words didn't fix the problem but they  gave me a new perspective big projects  or big goals may seem impossible in the  process because we get physically  exhausted and emotionally drained and we  also tend to get impatient because we  don't see the progress that we're making  when we're the ones running the race  what we did to combat this feeling of  running in place was to focus on smaller  tasks rather than the big picture so  instead of focusing on the giant  elephant in front of us in this case a  finished house we instead focused on  smaller tasks such as this week we will  lay flooring and actually i share more  information on my previous video so  check that one out if you want to know  more information about how to go about  setting goals if you have big projects  in mind look for ways to break them into  smaller chunks this can help you feel a  sense of accomplishment as you actually  achieve these steps instead of feeling  weighed down because you haven't yet  arrived to your end result but before we  go on i want to know what goals do you  have for this year let me know in the  comments lesson number two self-care is  a must not a maybe initially we thought  that we could both work our full-time  jobs work on the house on the weekends  and any day that we were off early  manage our business and manage our  personal lives and after a few months of  this it was physically and emotionally  draining and not only that but my  husband actually ended up injured he had  to take two weeks of work off unpaid and  this not only set us back as far as the  house project went and all of the uh  progress that we had already completed  but then we had added medical bills on  top of that what i mean by all of this  is that if you put your health on the  back burner thinking when i finish this  i'll rest more or once this is over i'll  eat better or once i get through this  i'll start exercising  you might not live to get there or you  may just get there only to find yourself  ill and not able to enjoy the lifestyle  that you thought you would have because  you focused on the end result  more than the process of actually  getting there be careful that you don't  take your ambitions to extremes because  unfortunately some people will find  themselves working extremely hard  throughout their lives and skimping on  their health in the process only to find  themselves paying for it all back and  then some in medical expenses and their  health is not something that they can  necessarily recover my husband talks  about a man that he once knew that  actually used to say this that he would  eat the banana peels because he paid for  that too and this was a person who  worked extremely hard day in and day out  but he would skimp on his health in  order to save money he actually did  accomplish his dream or what he thought  was his dream and he became a  millionaire and he had all the things  that he wanted but he did not achieve  the lifestyle that he had hoped for he  ended up dying early in sickness my  husband says that he knew him at the  time when he was in his death bed and he  said now i have all the money that i  ever wanted but i can't even eat salt  the cheapest of foods so make your  health a priority and stop making  excuses for why you can't it matters now  lesson number three those who succeed  learn to adapt people often tell me how  nice that you could build your own house  and have everything the way that you  wanted and well that wasn't exactly the  case anybody that's ever built a house  will know that you have to be able to  adapt to change and really i think it  applies to life as well rarely is there  ever going to be a situation where  everything just falls into place and  everything just happens perfectly the  way that we had planned for an example  that i can relate to you about our house  is that we had a three inch mistake in  our framing just three inches but that  completely threw off our kitchen  cabinetry we the layout that we had and  the piping there was not a cabinet that  we could fit within the corner of our  walls and we had to figure out a way to  work around that because we looked and  looked and we didn't have the money to  pay for custom and so that is actually  how we ended up with our floating  shelves so we found a way to work around  this situation to make it work for our  benefit instead of being stressed out of  uh now what are we going to do so it  wasn't what we had planned i didn't at  all expect that we would have a floating  shelf that wasn't what i envisioned but  we found a way to work around that  problem and adapt there will be times in  your life when things do not go the way  that you plan and adapting to those  situations can often imply sacrifice the  point is not to get stuck in a pity  party and leave the project altogether  it's about looking at the situation and  accepting it for what it is then adapt  lesson number four all work and no play  destroys relationships by this i'm  mainly speaking to people in  relationships but i think that it can  also apply to friendships as well when  we were building our house my mentor  warned me that starting a big project  like building a house or starting a  business is often the cause of divorce  and this idea was honestly strange to me  and me being the nerd that i am i  researched into it and to my surprise  she was correct this topic is quite  large and probably deserves a video of  its own so for now i will only talk to  you about two things that you should  watch out for just like we mentioned in  lesson number two if you become so  obsessively focused on a project that  you don't even take care of your own  self  what does that say about the  relationships around you  are people getting the best version of  you when you're around or are they  getting a grumpy tired complaining half  asleep seep warmer and number two are  you actually present and i use this word  intentionally because just because  you're in a room doesn't mean that  you're actually there and present in  conversation with the people that are  around you and this is actually  something that my husband and i  struggled with when we were building the  house because it seemed like we couldn't  be in the same room together in any kind  of situation and not talk about the  house it truly became an obsession and  having goals and projects and ambitions  is wonderful it's great but sometimes  without even realizing it we can get  into this gray zones and distance  ourselves from other people and before  we even know it we've missed out on our  relationships so take care of your  relationships nurture your relationships  because truly that's all that we have i  assure you that if you live in a  bajillion dollar house but you're all  alone and you have nobody to talk to  nobody to relate with that would feel  pretty darn lonely so take care of the  people that you have around you do still  follow your goals and pursue those goals  but make time for play schedule quality  time with the people that you love and  be present and if you can shut phones  and technology off during that time even  better and lastly lesson number five the  diligent work once and the lazy work  twice does it seem a bit odd that a lazy  person would work twice as hard as  someone else let me explain have you  ever tried to bring all your groceries  into the house at once because you  wanted to avoid having two trips and  then have a bacteria and food roll all  over the place this actually happened to  me a couple years back when we lived in  a downhill area and i had to scavenge  around trying to grab all of my  groceries as my neighbors were just  probably looking at me like this crazy  lady i had to run all the yard trying to  get my groceries only because i didn't  want to make two trips to grab my bag  and put it in the house anyone else ever  done that like come on i'm not the only  one am i and i think that the same  applies to big projects and just life in  general because when we take shortcuts  or put little effort in what we do not  only does it leave little hope that  we'll actually achieve greatness but  it's much more likely that things will  go wrong think about it this way if you  buy a product or a service from somebody  and the product is sloppy and thrown  together or done halfway you're probably  not going to purchase from them again if  you want to succeed in your major goals  excellence has to be where you set the  bar so those are my five lessons to  share with you for today i hope that you  found this video helpful and if so  please give it a thumbs up and subscribe  so that you won't miss when i post a new  video and let us know in the comments  what are some things that you do to help  you achieve your goals please share in  the comments so that we can all learn  from each other i hope you achieve all  your goals and then some thank you so  much for watching and i can't wait to  hear from you in the comments and see  you in the next video bye for now  [Music]  you

